  "research_interests": "Unpacking the drivers of solar PV cost decline (cost-driver decomposition in the style of Kavlak, McNerney and Trancik 2018): which low-level variables (module efficiency, polysilicon/silicon usage and price, wafer thickness, silver and glass inputs, plant size and economies of scale, manufacturing yield, labour and energy inputs) explain module, inverter, balance-of-system, soft-cost and LCOE changes; learning curves / Wright's law versus R&D, scale and spillovers as explanations; cost of capital/WACC and financing; supply-chain structure, Chinese manufacturing scale-up, overcapacity, trade measures (tariffs, anti-dumping, IRA local-content) and industrial organisation of the PV value chain (market structure, pricing below cost, input-output / value-added accounting); comparable decompositions for wind, batteries, electrolysers. Also valuable: public datasets of PV prices and bills of materials, and methods transferable to other technologies.",
